\author{Compiled by Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5) for Andr\'as Kornai}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Gbagyi (ISO 639-3: gbr; Glottocode: gbag1258) is a Niger-Congo language of Nigeria with about 700,000 speakers, classed as endangered. Joshua Project reports a larger ethnic population of about 1,472,000 and notes eastern and western groups speaking different languages. Resources found are few.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textit{Gbagyi Boda} (2014) by Donaye Shekwolo, Samtom Creation, a reading and writing primer covering the alphabet, consonant-vowel combinations and topical vocabulary: \url{https://nigeriareposit.nln.gov.ng/items/9932ec80-a564-438d-81d4-5131afd63ed0/full}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item J. A. Shekwo, \textit{Fundamentals of the Gbagyi Language} (1979, Ahmadu Bello University, Zaria), bibliographic record: \url{https://reflex.cnrs.fr/Lexiques/webball/biblio_bas.php?id=18418}
\end{itemize}
No dictionary was found.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Gbagyi Contemporary Bible on YouVersion: \url{https://www.bible.com/versions/4607}
\item Joshua Project profile, Gbagyi in Nigeria: \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/11839}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Global Recordings Network, Gbagyi: Vwezhi (film and Words of Life listings): \url{https://glorecnet-website.k.globalrecordings.net/en/language/10087}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
A primer and a Bible text exist, which gives a basis for early literacy. The grammar is a 1979 item whose content was not examined. No school programme was found, and a dictionary and graded readers would be needed.

\end{document}
